    description: "WHY. smart-test spends 311 to 370 s of every pre-PR cycle on a whole-repo analysis (\"the slice\") before any test runs. Walking an OLDER graph named the same test files in 741 historical pairs and 9 live comparisons, with no missed test file. But a stored graph does not last: each is a 333 MB survey file in a cache that evicts (12 of the 14 registered since 2026-11-16 are gone), and a worktree has its own cache and never finds one.\n\nWHAT (owner ruling on decision 15: option b, built BEFORE the switch). Whenever an analysis completes, write its graph into the existing selection index as rows: a symbol table keyed by stable_id and an edge table of integer triples. Add an in-process walk from a set of seed FILES to the test files that reach them. Prototype figures: 3.6 MB, 0.1 s to load, 2 ms per walk, against 4.8 s for `hypergumbo slice --files F --input <survey>`.\n\nRULES THE EVIDENCE ALREADY FIXES. Rows, not bitmaps (a compressed two-level bitmap is 0.91 MB against 1.06 MB for plain pairs; a flat one is 546 MB). Walk symbols, not files (the file walk names 4.5 times as many test files). No name-matching of old unresolved references (it added 203 wrong test files and found nothing). Seed by file path, not by symbol id (Symbol.id holds line numbers; stable_id changes when a signature does).\n\nCHECK FIRST. `selection_index.stored_edges` and `selection_index._bitmap` existed (2026-11-13 and 11-15) and were retired in PR #2217 as callables only their own tests reached. Read that history before writing new code: part of this may be a revert.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The row walk is a NEW reader of the graph; the shadow evidence was measured on `slice --input`. So: for every survey still on disk and for each seed set in the shadow log (`changed_source` in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stale_graph_observations.jsonl), the row walk names exactly the test files `hypergumbo slice --files F --input <that survey>` names; state the count of comparisons and of differences. A mutation of the walk turns its test red.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 5196
    fields: {}  # 5196
